BEGIN
CREATE EXTENSION
SET
1..26
ok 1 - the persistent vehicle trim cache exists
ok 2 - the cache stores only its bounded lookup, result, claim, and timestamp fields
ok 3 - row level security is enabled on the private cache
ok 4 - the private cache has no browser-facing RLS policies
ok 5 - all application roles are fenced away from direct cache table access
ok 6 - the race-safe cache claim RPC exists
ok 7 - the token-bound cache completion RPC exists
ok 8 - the token-bound cache release RPC exists
ok 9 - cache RPCs are security-definer functions with an empty search path
ok 10 - only the server service role can invoke the cache RPC surface
TRUNCATE TABLE
SET
ok 11 - the first request atomically claims an unseen vehicle
ok 12 - an ambiguous retry with the same token remains idempotently claimed
ok 13 - a concurrent token cannot start duplicate generation
ok 14 - a non-owner token cannot complete another request claim
ok 15 - the claim owner can persist the generated trim list
ok 16 - completion is idempotent after an ambiguous response
ok 17 - later requests receive the stored result immediately
RESET
ok 18 - the normalized primary key prevents duplicate cache rows
SET
ok 19 - an unknown lineup can be claimed normally
ok 20 - an empty high-confidence result is persistently cached
ok 21 - cached empty results also prevent repeat generation
ok 22 - a separate vehicle receives its own claim
ok 23 - a non-owner token cannot release a claim
ok 24 - a failed generator can release its own pending claim
ok 25 - a released failed claim can be retried later
RESET
UPDATE 1
SET
ok 26 - an expired abandoned claim can be recovered without a duplicate row
ROLLBACK
